.TH "historyofvideogamein4k-by-jean-yveslamoureux" "6" "2026-11-14" "History of video game in 4k User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
historyofvideogamein4k-by-jean-yveslamoureux - the command to run
History of video game in 4k.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
historyofvideogamein4k-by-jean-yveslamoureux [\f[B]--fullscreen\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
History of video game in 4k is a 4k intro written in ANSI C by Jean-Yves
Lamoureux for the 4k source compo of 2004.
It is a brief history of video games, from the 70\[cq]s to the 90\[cq]s,
in less than 4096 bytes of source code: a title in bitmap font, a pong,
a road (vroom), a raycaster (doom), and a scroller whose text is the
name of the source file.
.PP
The intro runs in a 640x480 window, without sound, and stops by itself
after about 2 minutes 10 seconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
--fullscreen
Start in fullscreen
.SH KEYS
.TP
Escape
Quit (closing the window also quits)
.TP
Any other key
Skip to the next part
.SH NOTES
.PP
The Debian version enables V-Sync (SDL12COMPAT_SYNC_TO_VBLANK=1, unless
already set in the environment): the pong moves one step per frame, and
it would last a fraction of a second without V-Sync.
.SH INFOS
.PP
https://320x200.org/2004/4k/
.SH BUGS
.PP
No known bugs.
